  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements: one is labelled as <strong>Assertion A</strong> and the other is labelled as <strong>Reason</strong> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">R</mi></math></p><p><strong>Assertion A</strong>: In an Ellingham diagram, the oxidation of carbon to carbon monoxide shows a negative slope with respect to temperature.</p><p><strong>Reason R</strong>: CO tends to get decomposed at higher temperature.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "aYGk7",
      "text": "&nbsp;Both A and R are correct and R is the correct explanation of A",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Zi2bL",
      "text": "A is not correct but R is correct",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "3qLTx",
      "text": "(3) Both A and R are correct but R is NOT the correct explanation of A",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "FyQD0",
      "text": "A is correct but R is not correct",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>CO</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>As the number of moles of gas increases entropy increases.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi>ve</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><msub><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p>Slope =&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math>&nbsp;=&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>ve</mi></math></p><p>As temperature increases <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> becomes more negative thus it has lower tendency to get decomposed.</p><p>Hence, A is correct but R is not correct.</p>",
